# Frontend (React 19 + Tauri)

- Call the Rust core with `invoke<T>("command_name")` from `@tauri-apps/api/core`.
  Keep backend calls centralized in `src/hooks/useTorApp.ts` rather than scattered
  across pages.
- Shared types live in `src/lib/types.ts` and must match the Rust command
  signatures. Import with the `@/` alias (configured in `tsconfig.json` / `vite.config.ts`).
- The UI is presentational: it renders status and sends typed commands. Never
  implement routing / firewall / secret logic in the UI, and never display or
  store onion keys, client credentials, bridge lines, or public IPs beyond what
  the backend already redacts.
- Components are functional only. Reuse primitives in `src/components/ui/*`; pages
  live in `src/pages/*`. Style with Tailwind v4 and `cn()` from `@/lib/utils`.
- User-facing strings go through `@/lib/i18n`; respect `dir` (fa = RTL).
- Connection presets live in `src/lib/presets.ts`.
